# DocStruct Cursor Rule

When creating, updating, or auditing documentation:

- Read existing docs before writing.
- Update existing files before creating new files.
- Create a new doc only when it has a clear responsibility.
- Keep one source of truth for each durable fact.
- Link instead of copying details.
- Mark uncertain information as `UNKNOWN`.
- Mark required work as `TODO`.
- Keep docs short unless complexity requires detail.
- Do not invent missing implementation details.
- Avoid empty placeholder files.

Use the smallest structure that preserves clarity, ownership, and continuity.
